1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:05,129
Antarctica just sent us a warning... and for 13 years, nobody heard it.

2
00:00:06,129 --> 00:00:15,199
Hidden in seismic data from the bottom of the world, scientists have just uncovered hundreds of secret earthquakes shaking the frozen continent.

3
00:00:16,199 --> 00:00:24,859
The discovery, published just days ago, reveals 362 hidden glacial quakes between 2010 and 2023.

4
00:00:25,859 --> 00:00:33,579
And 245 of them cluster at one terrifying location — the marine edge of Thwaites... the Doomsday Glacier.

5
00:00:34,580 --> 00:00:43,880
These are no ordinary earthquakes. They strike when icebergs the size of skyscrapers snap off, capsize, and slam into the glacier like battering rams.

6
00:00:44,880 --> 00:00:55,060
The signals are so low in frequency that global sensors missed them for over a decade. It took Antarctica's own seismic stations to finally hear the ice... screaming.

7
00:00:56,060 --> 00:01:06,820
And here's the chilling part. The quakes spiked exactly when Thwaites' floating ice tongue accelerated toward the sea — a sign the ocean itself may be destabilizing the ice.

8
00:01:07,820 --> 00:01:14,100
If Thwaites collapses completely, global sea levels rise by three meters. Entire coastlines... redrawn.

9
00:01:15,100 --> 00:01:21,220
For twenty years, we thought Antarctica was seismically silent. The truth? We just weren't listening.

10
00:01:22,220 --> 00:01:30,640
Now, every capsizing iceberg is a heartbeat we can measure — a countdown we can finally hear. Follow, for more from the edge of the world.
